ption=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>The <strong>XOR total=
</strong> of an array is defined as the bitwise <code>XOR</code> of<strong>=
 all its elements</strong>, or <code>0</code> if the array is<strong> empty=
</strong>.</p>

<ul>
	<li>For example, the <strong>XOR total</strong> of the array <code>[2,5,6]=
</code> is <code>2 XOR 5 XOR 6 =3D 1</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Given an array <code>nums</code>, return <em>the <strong>sum</strong> of=
 all <strong>XOR totals</strong> for every <strong>subset</strong> of </em>=
<code>nums</code>.&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Note:</strong> Subsets with the <strong>same</strong> elements s=
hould be counted <strong>multiple</strong> times.</p>

<p>An array <code>a</code> is a <strong>subset</strong> of an array <code>b=
</code> if <code>a</code> can be obtained from <code>b</code> by deleting s=
ome (possibly zero) elements of <code>b</code>.</p>

